@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: Patcher UAT Diagnostic
	Attempting to diagnose the status file issue by running a duplicate test without the teardown.

Scenario: Create a 71 build with public and private child builds
	@ test.group = "1"
	As a TSE, I should be able to create a 7.1 build containing both public and private child builds

	Given I log into the Patcher homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "liferay"
	And I generate random fix content for the first fix
	And I generate random fix content for the second fix
	And I create a Patcher fix with the following values
	| Product         | DXP 7.1                                             |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-8-7110-private                         |
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent1}                                |
	| Branch Name     | fix-pack-LPP-33279-dxp-8-private                    |
	| Github URL      | git@github.com:jonathanmccann/liferay-portal-ee.git |
	And I create a Patcher fix with the following values
	| Product         | DXP 7.1                                          |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-4-7110                              |
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent2}                             |
	| Branch Name     | LPS-89633-dxp-4                                  |
	| Github URL      | git@github.com:kenduenwald/liferay-portal-ee.git |
	| Workaround      | true                                             |
	And I wait for "5" seconds
	Then I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}" and type "Patch" with the following values
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent1}        |
	| Version         | 1.0                         |
	| Product         | DXP 7.1                     |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-8-7110-private |
	| Patcher Status  | Adding                      |
	| Type            | Patch                       |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent2}" and type "Workaround" with the following values
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent2} |
	| Version         | 1.0                  |
	| Product         | DXP 7.1              |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-4-7110  |
	| Patcher Status  | Adding               |
	| Type            | Workaround           |
	When I check the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}" and type "Patch" for add completion
	And I check the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent2}" and type "Workaround" for add completion
	Then I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}" and type "Patch" with the following values
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent1}        |
	| Version         | 1.0                         |
	| Product         | DXP 7.1                     |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-8-7110-private |
	| Git Hash        | 0e7e9a2cd4                  |
	| Patcher Status  | Complete                    |
	| Type            | Patch                       |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat)  |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent2}" and type "Workaround" with the following values
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent2}       |
	| Version         | 1.0                        |
	| Product         | DXP 7.1                    |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-4-7110        |
	| Git Hash        | ba56d593d1                 |
	| Patcher Status  | Complete                   |
	| Type            | Workaround                 |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat) |
	When I generate a random ticket number
	And I create a Patcher build for a new account with the following values
	| Product         | DXP 7.1                                   |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-8-7110                       |
	| Tickets List    | ${staticFixContent2},${staticFixContent1} |
	| Account Code    | DOEWAIKON                                 |
	| Support Ticket  | ${staticTicketNumber}                     |
	And I set the account code "DOEWAIKON" as a static variable
	And I wait for "5" seconds
	Then I should be able to view a Patcher build for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "DOEWAIKON" with the following values
	| Type            | Official                |
	| Support Ticket  | ${staticTicketNumber}   |
	| Version         | 1.0                     |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-8-7110     |
	| Content         | 0 Fix Packs + 2 Tickets |
	| Patcher Status  | Rebasing                |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher child build with the name "${staticFixContent1}" for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "DOEWAIKON" with the following values
	| Version         | 1.0                         |
	| Name            | ${staticFixContent1}        |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-8-7110-private |
	| Patcher Status  | Merging Only                |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher child build with the name "${staticFixContent2}" for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "DOEWAIKON" with the following values
	| Version         | 1.0                   |
	| Name            | ${staticFixContent2}  |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-8-7110   |
	| Patcher Status  | Rebasing Merging Only |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher child build fix with the name "${staticFixContent1}" for the child build with the name "${staticFixContent1}" for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "DOEWAIKON" with the following values
	| Name            | ${staticFixContent1} |
	| Version         | 1.0                  |
	| Git Hash        | 0e7e9a2cd4           |
	| Status          | Complete             |
	| Type            | Patch                |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher child build fix with the name "${staticFixContent2}" for the child build with the name "${staticFixContent2}" for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "DOEWAIKON" with the following values
	| Name            | ${staticFixContent2} |
	| Version         | 1.0                  |
	| Type            | Rebase               |
	When I check the Patcher build for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "DOEWAIKON" for rebase completion
	And I check the Patcher build for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "DOEWAIKON" for merge completion
	And I check the Patcher build for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "DOEWAIKON" for compile completion using the "fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(uat)" Jenkins job
	Then I should be able to view a Patcher build for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "DOEWAIKON" with the following values
	| Type            | Official                           |
	| Support Ticket  | ${staticTicketNumber}              |
	| Version         | 1.0                                |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-8-7110                |
	| Content         | 0 Fix Packs + 2 Tickets            |
	| Patcher Status  | Complete                           |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(uat)     |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat)         |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher child build with the name "${staticFixContent1}" for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "DOEWAIKON" with the following values
	| Version         | 1.0                            |
	| Name            | ${staticFixContent1}           |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-8-7110-private    |
	| Patcher Status  | Complete Merging Only          |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat)     |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(uat) |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher child build with the name "${staticFixContent2}" for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "DOEWAIKON" with the following values
	| Version         | 1.0                        |
	| Name            | ${staticFixContent2}       |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-8-7110        |
	| Patcher Status  | Complete Merging Only      |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat) |